    {
      "name": "write_review",
      "args": {
        "content": "# Security Review \u2014 pass1\n\n## Summary\nThis brownfield `feature-new` run introduces per-character-range text colors and highlights (`element.textStyles`) across `@excalidraw/element` and `@excalidraw/excalidraw`, including range normalization/shifting, bidi run projection, canvas and SVG rendering, WYSIWYG preview overlay, scene restore, and Stroke/Highlight color picker actions. DOM rendering in `textWysiwyg.tsx` and `<tspan>` text emission in `staticSvgScene.ts` safely use `textContent` and DOM APIs rather than `innerHTML`. However, two security issues in `packages/element/src/textStyles.ts` affect untrusted scene/collaboration payloads restored via `restore.ts`: (1) `sanitizeStyleColor` and `sanitizeStyleHighlight` accept arbitrary non-empty strings without validating that they are CSS colors, allowing SVG `<FuncIRI>` paint server values such as `url(...)` to be written raw into `<rect fill>` and `<tspan fill>` during light-mode SVG export; and (2) `normalizeTextRanges` / `buildNormalizedRanges` place no cap on input range count and perform quadratic $O(B \\times N)$ work over range boundaries, enabling main-thread CPU denial of service on crafted payloads. Additionally, two out-of-scope files (`ColorPicker.tsx` and `LayerUI.tsx`) interact with `actionChangeTextHighlight`'s `type=\"elementBackground\"` / `openPopup` aliasing to preview EyeDropper picks as `backgroundColor` on selected elements (such as a sticky note's fill while editing its label).\n\n## Findings\n| Severity | Category | Location | Issue | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Medium | Input Validation / SVG Paint Injection | `packages/element/src/textStyles.ts:34-63`, `packages/excalidraw/renderer/staticSvgScene.ts:842-881` | `sanitizeStyleColor` and `sanitizeStyleHighlight` only trim strings and reject `\"\"` / `\"transparent\"`, allowing arbitrary strings from untrusted files or collaboration peers (`packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts:579`) to persist in `element.textStyles`. In light-mode SVG export"
      },
      "canonical_path": null,
      "args_clipped": true
    }
